From 1400bc88073e86c4412d89f05fe7d0ca74db7612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: ralink: mt7620: keep the kernel code out of the first
 32 KiB

The 24KEc of the MT7620 (PRId 0x00019650) can save a wrong EPC for an
interrupt taken at the first instruction of a J or JAL target: bits
31:28 of the EPC then come from the address of the delay slot plus the
sign-extended low 16 bits of the jump, as if it were a branch. This
happens when bits 19 and 16 of the jump are set. Within a 256 MiB
segment it gives a different result only for a jump in the first
32 KiB, and then the return from the interrupt goes to the right
offset in the segment below: 0x7... instead of 0x8..., and the kernel
dies with "Unable to handle kernel paging request" in kernel mode.

The kernel is linked at 0x80000000, so its first 32 KiB hold the early
and the cold code (.text.unlikely), with calls that run often enough
to hit this: try_to_generate_entropy() during boot, arch_align_stack()
on exec.

The 24Kc of an AR9132 does the same (seen from user space, which has
the same problem in its own first 32 KiB of a segment), so this looks
like an erratum of the 24K core; ath79 loads its kernel at 0x80060000
and never runs code there.

MediaTek's SDK kernels leave the same 32 KiB empty with
". = . + 0x8000" at the start of .text in vmlinux.lds.S: for all SoCs
in its 2.6.36 kernel, only for MT7620 and MT7628 in its 3.10 kernel.

Raise the space before _stext from 0x400 to 0x8000 bytes on MT7620.
This costs 31 KiB of RAM.

Measured on a TL-WPA7510 v2 with a loop of JALs: about 20 such EPCs a
second from 0x80003f90, none from 0x80008f90 and above, none with
interrupts disabled, none with JALR to the same target. Before this,
6 of 17 boots crashed; after it, none of 15 did.

Signed-off-by: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/kernel/head.S | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/head.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/head.S
@@ -66,8 +66,17 @@
 	 * Reserved space for exception handlers.
 	 * Necessary for machines which link their kernels at KSEG0.
 	 */
+#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_MT7620
+	/*
+	 * The 24KEc of the MT7620 can save an EPC with wrong top four bits
+	 * for an interrupt at the target of a J or JAL in the first 32 KiB
+	 * of a 256 MiB segment, so keep the kernel code out of there.
+	 */
+	.fill	0x8000
+#else
 	.fill	0x400
 #endif
+#endif
 
 EXPORT(_stext)
 
